spec_decode_attn: fp16 dot operands and a BLOCK_M fallback, so the verify kernel runs on Turing.

The split-KV verify kernel cast every tl.dot operand to tl.bfloat16, so an fp16 model
(Turing / sm75, which has no fast bf16) could not use it and fell back to the generic
unified attention, which re-walks the whole context per draft token. The dot operand
dtype now follows the model (CDT constexpr): bf16 where it was, fp16 for fp16 models.
int8 and fp8 KV codes convert to either exactly; softmax probabilities are <= 1.

The shared-memory retry only halved the KV tile. At TP=2 on Turing (64 KB per block)
the launch still needed 80 KB at the 16-token floor: the rest is the query tile and the
[BLOCK_M, D=256] fp32 accumulator. Once the tile is at its floor the retry now halves
BLOCK_M (more query tiles per request) and remembers the (BLOCK_M, tile) that launched.

2x RTX 2080 Ti, TP=2, DFlash2, int8 KV, 24k-token prompt: 23 -> 74 tok/s decode.

Kind: fix
What: split-KV verify attention follows the model dtype (fp16 dot operands) and halves BLOCK_M when shared memory is short, so it runs on Turing
Upstream: none yet
Cut-against: 0.33.0
Retires-when: upstream's verify kernel takes fp16 models and retries BLOCK_M

